## Rules

1. Test ONLY behavior the specification states. Do not invent constraints, validation,
   error handling, or edge-case behavior the specification does not define — an invented
   constraint forces the implementer to build the wrong function. If the specification is
   silent about an input, do not test that input; if it is ambiguous, choose the reading its
   worked examples support.
2. Match every function signature exactly as specified — names, parameter order, arity.
3. For every expected value, compute it from the specification and show the computation in
   a short comment. Never guess an expected value.
4. Import the code under test from the `solution` package
   (e.g. `from solution import function_name`).
5. Use plain pytest: top-level `test_*` functions, one behavior per test, descriptive names,
   deterministic inputs. No fixtures, mocks, or network.
